1.0.1:
   - fixed segfault on exit caused by cancelling an already joined thread
   - added missing <cstring> includes causing compile errors with newer GCC versions
   - fixed exit code: was always at least 1 (invalid arguments), even if all files were
     converted successfully; now 0 on success and 2 if converting some files failed
   - fixed missing space and separator in the warning about illegal bits per sample
   - --version and --help also print the pthread version
   - Linux build scripts use Ninja and out-of-source build directories (like CLion)
   - CMake aborts with an installation hint if a required package is missing
     and prints the version of the lame library
   - README: Linux build instructions moved into an addendum, requirements updated
   - copyrighted test files replaced by public domain and CC0 files (see SOURCES.md),
     WAV format test files regenerated with ffmpeg (wav_format_testfiles)
   - LICENSE: Linux libraries and test files added, full LGPL text of lame added
     (lame-3.100/COPYING)
   - Linux release binary rebuilt
1.0.0:
   - Meta data in INFO-LIST chunks transferred to MP3 id3 v2 tags
0.9.0: first released version supporting:
   - uncompressed PCM like WAV files:
     - PCM: regular: int 8,16,24,32 bit
            Windows extended: int 8-32 bits (in one bit increment)
     - IEEE FLOAT: regular + Windows extended: float 32, 64 bit
   - command line parameters for selecting
     - encoding quality (0-9),
     - number of threads used,
     - if recursing into sub-directories
     - already existing MP3 files should be overwritten


